device-to-host copies, and CPU post-processing. With 623 AIRs generating over 1200 kernel launches per segment, launch overhead alone accounts for roughly 62ms, before even counting the data transfers and CPU work. A batch descriptor-array approach would collapse all these small AIRs into a single kernel launch, eliminating most of this overhead.\n\nI'm committing to the batch Round 0 descriptor-array kernels optimization despite the two previous failures, because the situation is different now. The first attempt failed due to Rust optimizer interference, which the caller-routing approach fixed. The second hit OOM from too many kernel template instantiations, but I can mitigate that by using runtime branching instead of compile-time templates and being more selective about which variants to add. The infrastructure is already well-understood from the earlier work, so I'm not starting from scratch. With 14 optimizations already delivering 1.79x speedup, Round 0 is the clearest path to meaningful gains.\n\nThe 161ms bottleneck is too significant to leave unaddressed. I'm targeting 100-150ms improvement at APC 300, bringing it down from 241ms. The probability is medium since I understand what went wrong before, and the complexity is high because it requires careful CUDA and Rust coordination with tight GPU memory constraints.\n\nActually, I need to be more precise here—the second failure was OOM in the GKR input allocation, not in Round 0 itself. That happened because the clean CUDA rebuild added new kernel templates that bloated static GPU memory. The current code runs APC 300 fine, so the issue is specifically about which new kernel variants I introduce. I need to be surgical about template instantiations to avoid pushing past the memory budget again.\n\nThe key is using `__launch_bounds__` and converting template parameters like `NEEDS_SHMEM` and `IS_IDENTITY_COSET` to runtime conditionals instead. That way I get the performance gains without the memory explosion.\n\nNow I'm ready to formalize the ideas list, pick the top candidate, and write out the task and plan documents. Let me pull up the spec.py metrics one more time to verify the current Round 0 timing and check if I have per-segment breakdowns available.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":964,"cache_read_input_tokens":144118,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":964},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"50e92e47-0cd3-4f35-91c1-5f23da5f72d3","uuid":"84bf1e6b-d978-4f92-b7a4-34606a75be88"}
