{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"You are reviewing an optimization plan for a GPU prover. Read the following files, then review the plan according to the review guideline. Return your response in the format: Findings, Improvements, Assessment.\n\nFiles to read:\n1. `/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt/review_guideline.md` — the review standard to follow\n2. `/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt/context.md` — project context\n3. `/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/task.md` — the task being planned\n4. `/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/2026-04-14-0030-rightsize-gkr-input-kernel-grid/plan.md` — the plan to review\n\nAdditionally, to verify claims in the plan, read these source files:\n- `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/gkr_input.cu` — the CUDA kernel and launcher\n- `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/gkr_input.rs` — the Rust-side orchestration\n\nThe plan claims a one-line CUDA fix will dramatically improve multi-stream concurrency for GKR input evaluation. Your job is to verify:\n1. Is the grid-sizing analysis correct? Does the current code really always launch 256 blocks for GLOBAL mode regardless of height?\n2. Is the intermediates buffer access pattern correct after the fix? Will reducing the stride break anything?\n3. Are the performance estimates realistic given the nsys data cited?\n4. Is the plan specific enough to implement without guessing?\n\nReview this plan following the review guideline. Return your response in the format: Findings, Improvements, Assessment."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_016G5vt4eUHuJJmDZiRwfvQj","session_id":"50e92e47-0cd3-4f35-91c1-5f23da5f72d3","uuid":"2259808b-b933-4a0a-b932-73cec8c47c18","timestamp":"2026-04-13T23:21:30.011Z"}
