{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QttNfGrViob6fK9otdnRZv","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# 2026-04-14-0030-rightsize-gkr-input-kernel-grid\n2\t\n3\tRight-size the GKR input evaluation kernel grid for small GLOBAL-mode AIRs. Currently, the CUDA launcher always uses `TASK_SIZE=65536` as the thread count for GLOBAL mode, launching 256 blocks regardless of the AIR's actual height. For the majority of AIRs at APC 300 (height << 65536), over 98% of threads exit immediately at the boundary check, yet each 256-block kernel saturates the RTX 4090's 128 SMs, preventing concurrent execution across the 8 multi-stream worker threads. Changing the launcher to use `min(TASK_SIZE, height)` allows small-AIR kernels to use proportionally fewer blocks (e.g., 4 blocks for height=1024 instead of 256), freeing SMs for concurrent kernel execution from other threads. This should dramatically improve multi-stream concurrency in GKR input eval — the single largest sub-component at APC 300 (seg0: 241ms, 17.6% of STARK excl trace).\n4\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01DHoVGqD9vyVwvZ1ttp9qXk","session_id":"50e92e47-0cd3-4f35-91c1-5f23da5f72d3","uuid":"37f2a13e-fcda-414e-89e0-1b41b8366512","timestamp":"2026-04-13T23:24:36.864Z"}
